## 8️⃣ Common pitfalls & how to fix them

| Symptom | Likely cause | Fix |
|---------|--------------|-----|
| **Map stays gray, console shows `Failed to load source`** | CORS header missing on the host. | Add `Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *` (or your domain) and `Access-Control-Allow-Headers: Range`. |
| **Tiles load at zoom 0‑14, then disappear at higher zoom** | You used `tiles: ['pmtiles://…/{z}/{x}/{y}']` instead of `url:`. | Switch to `url:` so the protocol reads the archive’s `maxzoom`. |
| **All vector layers are empty** | Wrong `source-layer` name. | Run `pmtiles show <file>` to list the exact layer names, then update the style. |
| **Slow first‑load, then fast** | The whole .pmtiles file is being downloaded (no Range support). | Verify the server returns `Accept-Ranges: bytes`. In S3, this is automatic; on some static hosts you may need to enable it. |
| **404 on tile request** | The URL is not publicly reachable (signed URL expired, bucket private). | Make the file public or generate a fresh signed URL. |
| **MapLibre throws “Protocol pmtiles not registered”** | `addProtocol` was called after the map was created. | Register the protocol **before** you instantiate any `new maplibregl.Map()`. |

